# AI Headquarters - Environment Variables

Copy this file to `.env.local` (development) or set the same names in the
Vercel project (production). Never commit real values.

## Required for Development

```bash
# Supabase Configuration
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key

# Application
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000
NODE_ENV=development
```

## Background job / cron

```bash
# Required for POST /api/jobs/tick to run at all; the endpoint fails closed
# (HTTP 503) when unset. Use a long random string and set the same value in the
# external scheduler (Vercel Cron, GitHub Actions, an uptime pinger, etc.).
CRON_SECRET=replace-with-a-long-random-secret
```

## Vercel AI Gateway (optional; used by the standalone index.ts example)
# Add the real value only to your local .env.local file; never commit it.
AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY=your-vercel-ai-gateway-key

# AI provider keys

Every AI key is OPTIONAL. An absent key yields an honest `requires_credential`
state in the UI -- never fabricated data. Configure at least one to collect real
answers.

```bash
# Business Brain generation + the "ChatGPT" monitoring surface
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-your-openai-api-key

# Optional: Business Brain generation
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your-anthropic-api-key

# Optional: Vercel AI Gateway (https://vercel.com/docs/ai-gateway)
# A routing layer that fronts many models behind one key. It is only used when
# neither OPENAI_API_KEY nor ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is set, because prompts sent
# through the gateway pass through Vercel's infrastructure. Model ids are
# "vendor/model"; only models listed in lib/ai/config/pricing.ts can be costed,
# and an unpriced model is refused rather than billed as untracked spend.
# AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY=your-ai-gateway-api-key
# AUTHORITY_GATEWAY_MODEL=moonshotai/kimi-k3
```

## AI Authority Engine -- monitoring surfaces (all OPTIONAL)

Each key enables one monitored AI surface. Absence is a supported state: the
engine records `requires_credential` and collects nothing from that surface.
`google_ai` has no authorized programmatic API and is reported `unsupported` by
design; it is never scraped.

```bash
# Perplexity (returns citations natively -- highest-signal source when set)
PERPLEXITY_API_KEY=

# Google Gemini
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# xAI Grok
XAI_API_KEY=

# Model overrides (optional; sensible defaults are compiled in)
AUTHORITY_CHATGPT_MODEL=gpt-4o
AUTHORITY_GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-1.5-pro
AUTHORITY_GROK_MODEL=grok-2
AUTHORITY_PERPLEXITY_MODEL=sonar

# Per-query provider timeout in ms (clamped 2000-120000; default 30000)
AUTHORITY_ADAPTER_TIMEOUT_MS=30000

# Website the crawler monitors. Falls back to organizations.website when unset.
AUTHORITY_SITE_ORIGIN=https://example.com

# Comma-separated domains treated as first-party (the subject business).
AUTHORITY_SUBJECT_DOMAINS=example.com
```

## AI Authority Engine -- external integrations (OPTIONAL, credential-gated)

Every integration reports `unconfigured` and syncs nothing until its credentials
are supplied. Obtaining a Google refresh token requires a one-time human consent
screen; see DEPLOYMENT_GUIDE.md and docs/CONNECTIONS-CHECKLIST.md for the
checklist.

```bash
# Google Search Console (OAuth refresh-token flow)
GOOGLE_SEARCH_CONSOLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_SEARCH_CONSOLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
GOOGLE_SEARCH_CONSOLE_REFRESH_TOKEN=

# Google Business Profile (OAuth refresh-token flow)
GOOGLE_BUSINESS_PROFILE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_BUSINESS_PROFILE_CLIENT_SECRET=
GOOGLE_BUSINESS_PROFILE_REFRESH_TOKEN=

# Google Analytics 4 (read-only Data API; scope analytics.readonly)
# Store the numeric GA4 property id per-org in
# authority_integrations.property_or_location (provider 'google_analytics_4').
GOOGLE_ANALYTICS_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_ANALYTICS_CLIENT_SECRET=
GOOGLE_ANALYTICS_REFRESH_TOKEN=

# GitHub repository status (READ-ONLY). Fine-grained token with Contents,
# Pull requests and Actions set to "read" on the target repo. Store owner/repo
# in authority_integrations.property_or_location (provider 'github_repository').
# GITHUB_TOKEN is used as a fallback when this is unset.
GITHUB_STATUS_TOKEN=
```

## Integration smoke test (never set in production)

```bash
# BUSINESS_BRAIN_SMOKE_FAKE_PROVIDER=1
```

## Supabase Storage Setup

1. Create a new bucket named `logos`
2. Set bucket visibility to public
3. Enable RLS policies

## AI Cost Tracking

All AI executions are automatically tracked:
- Input tokens
- Output tokens
- Estimated cost
- Execution time
- Provider and model used

## Budget Management

Set monthly AI budget per organization (default: $100):
- Tracked in `ai_usage_limits` table
- Checked before every execution
- Can be paused with "PAUSE ALL AI" kill switch

## Logging & Audit Trail

All operations logged in:
- `ai_execution_logs` - AI calls
- `activity_events` - All AI activity
- `approval_requests` - Pending decisions
- `task_outcomes` - Results and learnings
